## Additional permission for assessment and research verification

In addition to the licences above, any recipient may view, copy and internally circulate author-controlled materials, execute the author-controlled code, and reproduce the study's experiments or analyses solely for either of these purposes:

1. Assessing the author's fellowship, employment, research-funding or collaboration application or proposal.
2. Independently verifying or reproducing the study's reported methods and findings.

This permission applies to reviewers and researchers at commercial as well as noncommercial organizations, including when their assessment or verification work is paid. It includes configuring a local environment, making and recording changes reasonably necessary for reproduction, running the evaluation with appropriately obtained model access, and reporting verification findings with attribution to the Discovery Reasoning Study and disclosure of material changes. Running existing models to reproduce an evaluation is permitted; model-provider access, usage charges and terms remain the recipient's responsibility.

This additional permission does not itself authorize incorporation into commercial products, commercial deployment, providing paid services based on these materials, or training/fine-tuning models for commercial use. Such uses require separate permission unless already permitted by another applicable licence or by law. It conveys no third-party rights, implies no endorsement, and does not restrict rights already granted by the licences above or applicable law.

